;;; Executable ADR: the durable entity of a session is the conversation —
;;; conversation identity as a stored fact, and resume / fork as first-class vocabulary.

(require doeff-adr.macros [defadr defsemgrep rule law])
(import doeff-adr.macros [fact interpretation counterexample])


(defadr ADR-DOE-AGENTS-006
  :title "The durable entity of a session is the conversation (agent-native transcript) — promote conversation identity to a stored fact on the session row, and add resume / fork as first-class citizens of the effect vocabulary, RPC, and conformance"
  :status "accepted"
  :scope ["packages/doeff-agents (sessionhost: store / effects / launch / host / policy / impls)"
          "packages/doeff-agents/conformance"]
  :problem
    [(fact
       "The agent_sessions row has no agent-native conversation identity. Its columns are only session_id (the host's own ID) / session_name / pane_id / agent_type / work_dir / status / backend_kind / backend_ref_json (mux reference) / timestamps / pr_url / output_snippet / terminal_cause_json; neither claude's session UUID nor codex's rollout is stored. The host therefore structurally has no means to revive a conversation, and session kill = loss of the conversation is effectively the specification."
       :evidence "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/store.hy:62-78 (CREATE TABLE agent_sessions)")
     (fact
       "Neither the effect vocabulary nor the wire vocabulary has resume / fork. The kind surface has 5 terms: BuildLaunch / PreLaunchSetup / ClassifyPane / DeliverMessage / WireResultChannel; the RPCs are only session.launch / get / list / capture / send / cancel / cleanup / await_result / report_result, and the lifecycle is one-way: launch → terminal → cleanup."
       :evidence "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/effects.hy:172-215; dispatch in host.hy (daemon.status / kinds.list / session.*)")
     (fact
       "The native CLI physics of both kinds already provide resume and fork as first-class: claude has --session-id <uuid> (identity can be specified before startup) / --resume <id> / --fork-session (mints a new session ID on resume); codex has codex resume <SESSION_ID> / codex fork as subcommands (measured via --help on 2026-07-13). The missing abstraction is only on the sessionhost side."
       :evidence "claude --help / codex --help / codex resume --help (measured 2026-07-13)")
     (fact
       "There is already a proof on the consumer side: orch's ADR-0005 (2026-07-13) codified 'mux session = disposable cache, durable state = agent transcript, revivability is a stored fact' (LS2 / LS5) and implemented and verified the identity-capture physics (claude = mint UUID + --session-id / codex = discover rollout by cwd-match after boot) (orch PR #532). But the identity's home is orch's event log, not the sessionhost that owns the session, so ownership is split — other control planes such as ACP or conductor have no choice but to reimplement the same capture physics themselves (duplicate implementation of protocol physics = a replay of the structure ADR-DOE-AGENTS-004 diagnosed as the rot of the Rust/Python dual implementation)."
       :evidence "orch repo docs/adr/defadr_0005_run_session_lifecycle.hy; orch PR #532")
     (fact
       "[Driving problem of the 2026-08-11 revision] ACP (agent-control-plane) quota-exhaustion failover, per decision decision-acp-ratelimit-attempt-loss-2026-08-11 (option A adopted), requires resuming the same conversation under a different account, but session.resume could only reconstruct the binding from the source row's effective_identity, with no way for the caller to specify a different auth home. Also, the transcript's home (claude projects jsonl / codex rollout) is per auth home, so merely switching the home does not let the real CLI find the transcript (claude: 'No conversation found with session ID' rc=1; codex: 'no rollout found for thread id' rc=1 — resume-physics.md 2026-08-11 probes (a)(c)). Furthermore, a resume admission failure was a bare RuntimeError → {\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"<msg>\"} with no error_code, so machine consumers (the ACP Haskell client) had to rely on message substring matching."
       :evidence "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/launch.hy (binding reconstruction in resume-session); packages/doeff-agents/conformance/resume-physics.md (additional cross-binding probes)")
     (fact
       "[Driving problem of the 2026-08-18 revision] Not a single production resume had run to completion (agentd.sqlite: 105 rows with non-NULL resumed_from_session_id, 0 done, 2026-08-12 to 08-17). The primary cause for 91 of those rows was the disappearance of the host location: ACP deletes the workspace (.acp/workspaces/inv_wi_*) after an invocation ends, but resume failover reuses the source row's work_dir (fixed to the source copy) as is. sessionhost passed the work_dir to tmux without checking that it exists, and tmux silently substitutes $HOME for a missing start-directory — the pane's shell prompt comes up as `CA-…:~`. Because claude's --resume resolves the conversation by the cwd key (projects/<mangle(realpath cwd)>), it could not see the transcript at all, even though the transplant had laid it correctly, and died immediately with 'No conversation found with session ID' rc=1. The startup gate had no classification name for this screen and waited until the 120s budget ran out, terminating with no-agent-frame / prompt_undelivered (confirmed in 91/91 evidence frames — every one showed 'shell prompt at HOME + No conversation found'). This is a hole in the premise of R4: 'fixing to the source copy guarantees transcript discoverability' holds only while the work_dir exists."
       :evidence "~/.local/state/doeff/agentd.sqlite (cross-check of output_snippet for all 105 rows with non-NULL resumed_from, 2026-08-18); filed by fleet-stall-steward v143 route-de257d16f2; sessionhost-steward v215")]
  :context
    [(interpretation
       "Ontology: the durable entity is the conversation (agent-native transcript: claude's projects jsonl / codex's rollout), and a session row is one incarnation of it. resume = a new incarnation row with the same conversation ref (generation + 1). fork = a new row with a new conversation ref derived from the parent transcript. The finality of a terminal row is inviolable (a consequence of truth-is-rows) — rows are not revived; the conversation moves to a new row.")
     (interpretation
       "This continues the line of ADR-DOE-AGENTS-004, 'agentd = a mini control plane with the same ontology as ACP, requiring no new theory': session row = Pod (disposable, ends at terminal, recreated), conversation = persistent identity (isomorphic to a StatefulSet ordinal / PVC). It imports settled semantics rather than inventing.")
     (interpretation
       "Revivability is a stored fact; the FS or CLI is not probed at kill / reap decision time (imported from orch ADR-0005 LS2 / LS5). The identity being written on the row is the definition of resumable. Probing creates TOCTOU and a split of authority (which is the truth, the row or the FS).")]
  :decision
    [(rule R1 "Conversation identity is a product of launch: every kind impl settles the conversation identity at startup and writes it to the session row. claude = the host mints a UUID and injects it with --session-id (settled before boot). codex = discover the rollout after boot (via Fs / Clock effects — impls stay substrate-clean; identify it by cwd-match on work_dir, and use the UUID in the rollout file name as the identity). Capture is kind-owned physics of BuildLaunch / PreLaunchSetup; a capture failure must not silently leave the session running without identity — it appears on the row as a typed degraded observation (identity-unknown), and a resume request for that session becomes a typed failure.")
     (rule R2 "schema: add to agent_sessions conversation_json (a kind-discriminated union: claude {session_id} / codex {session_id, rollout_path}), generation (incarnation ordinal, 1-based), and lineage (resume source session_id / fork parent session_id). An UPDATE that returns the status of a row that reached terminal to an active status is forbidden (the machine surface of the ontology). Existing rows migrate as generation=1 with unknown conversation, following the identity-unknown semantics (R1).")
     (rule R3 "effect vocabulary: add BuildResume [agent-type params] (mode = resume | fork is discriminated in params — the physics are on the same surface (argv construction) and capability advertisement uses the same axis, so it is not a separate effect). Physics: claude: --resume <uuid> (fork adds --fork-session) / codex: codex resume <uuid> / codex fork. argv physics are owned solely by the kind module in sessionhost impls/, and resume / fork are included in the scope of law protocol-physics-has-one-home (ADR-DOE-AGENTS-004). Hosting the incarnation (pane creation, env composition, result channel wiring) goes through the same shared policy program as launch — no resume-specific parallel implementation is created.")
     (rule R4 "RPC vocabulary: session.resume {session_id, prompt?} = create a new incarnation row of the same conversation (new session_id, generation + 1, lineage recorded). session.fork {session_id, prompt?} = a new row for a new conversation (generation = 1, fork parent recorded in lineage). A resume when a non-terminal incarnation of the same conversation already exists is a typed reject (one-live-incarnation). Whether fork is independent of the parent's liveness (can one fork while the parent is alive) depends on CLI physics, so the accepted form is settled by Phase 0 probe measurement before it is advertised. [2026-08-11 revision (ACP quota-exhaustion failover — decision decision-acp-ratelimit-attempt-loss-2026-08-11): session.resume accepts 3 optional params (all backward-compatible, resume-only; specifying them on fork is a fail-closed reject). (1) binding — a typed union of the same shape as session.launch. When specified, it overrides reconstruction from the source row's effective_identity. Admission shares the same implementation as launch's R7 admission (policy binding-admission-error); a duplicated implementation is forbidden. When the home differs, R7 (transplant) fires. (2) new_session_id — the caller mints the new incarnation's session_id (ACP uses the agent_<invocationId> convention). session_name is set to the same value. A collision with an existing id is rejected with the same vocabulary as launch (session is already registered), before any side effect. When unspecified, the existing server-minted <base>~g<N> is kept. The truth of lineage is always the resumed_from_session_id column; it is never derived from naming. (3) expected_result — the same payload_schema admission as launch (sharing the host's admit-expected-result). 'Specified' is decided by the presence of the key; when specified (including explicit null = no contract), it takes priority over carrying an unfulfilled contract; when unspecified, the contract is carried as before. work_dir is still not accepted — fixing to the source copy is the guarantee of transcript discoverability (projects/<mangled cwd>/ physics). [2026-08-18 addendum: this guarantee holds only while the work_dir physically exists — existence is an admission fact of R10.]]")
     (rule R5 "capability advertisement: add {resumable, forkable} to the per-kind advertisement of kinds.list and advance the api_version of the affected kind (ADR-DOE-AGENTS-004 R5 — changing the schema while keeping the version makes the versioned vocabulary hollow). resume / fork on an unsupported kind / identity-unknown row is a typed reject at admission. [2026-07-13 refinement at implementation time: api_version (BINDING-KIND-API-VERSION) is the contract version of the binding's accepted form, and the capability advertisement is an additive field on a separate axis — this change does not alter the accepted form, so the version stays. Advancing it would make ACP's verifyBindingKindsOnce report a false BindingKindUnsupported and wrongly drop registered bindings. The 'hollowing' of 004 R5 applies when the accepted form changes while the version stays; here the accepted form is unchanged. Machine surface: the BINDING-KIND-RESUMABLE / BINDING-KIND-FORKABLE tables in policy.hy + test-dispatch-kinds-list in sessionhost_host_deftests.hy (turns red on divergence between table and advertisement).]")
     (rule R6 "Conformance first (continuing ADR-DOE-AGENTS-004 R4): add the resume / fork contract (transcript inheritance, minting a new identity on fork) to the fake CLI, make the scenarios green first, then write the real CLI physics. Minimum bar: (a) kill → resume preserves the conversation context, (b) fork lineage recording and independence (the fork conversation survives killing the parent), (c) resume on an identity-unknown row is a typed failure, (d) rejection of concurrent incarnations, (e) monotonic increase of generation and generation consistency of await_result / report_result (a late report from an old incarnation does not pollute the new incarnation's result). Real CLI physics (especially the accepted form of codex fork and rollout inheritance, and the transcript semantics of claude --fork-session) are recorded as measurements in a Phase 0 probe document following the conformance/herdr-physics.md precedent before the impl is written. [2026-08-11 revision: the fake CLI makes resume without a transcript / rollout fail loudly as the real CLI does (claude 'No conversation found with session ID' / codex 'no rollout found for thread id', rc=1, no silent new conversation — mirroring resume-physics.md probes (a)(c)). S21 verifies over the wire the cross-binding resume golden (context inheritance across the transplant link, recording the new binding's effective_identity, new_session_id) and the typed reject for transcript-not-discoverable (no row created).]")
     (rule R7 "Transcript transplant preprocessing (added 2026-08-11): for a cross-binding resume (binding specified ∧ a home different from the source row's effective_identity), before launch the per-kind impl lays the transcript from the source home into the binding home via symlink. The physics are frozen by the resume-physics.md 2026-08-11 probe: claude = projects/<mangle(canonical work_dir)>/<conversation.session_id>.jsonl + 3 pairs of surrounding artifacts (sessions-index.json / session-env/<sid> / file-history/<sid> — isomorphic to the 4 pairs of dotfiles agentcli share.py; only the transcript is required, the surroundings are best-effort). codex = link the rollout_path of conversation_json to <target sessions root>/<same relative path under sessions/> (native form = codex_home/sessions, two-axis form = profile_dir/sessions) — codex's resume discovery always scans its own home's sessions/, and the CLI does not follow the absolute rollout_path. If the source transcript is absent both as an entity and as a symlink target, it is a typed reject (transcript_not_discoverable) — moving the real CLI's loud failure earlier, before row creation. The transplant's path physics are owned solely by the kind module in sessionhost impls/ (an extension of law resume-physics-has-one-home), and the only substrate primitive is FsLinkArtifact (a semantic port of share.py link_session_artifact: source-missing / same-entity no-op / target-conflict no-op / linked / refused-by-container). [2026-09-22 revision (design docs/design/symlink-verbs-fail-vocabulary-ZCN5BD): added refused-by-container to the vocabulary and made the return value an FsSymlinkOutcome carrying state / errno / detail. The forms in which the container (file system) refuses the laying — permission / capacity / read-only / an entity at the parent's position / a same-instant collision — are bound to happen yet were not in the 4-value vocabulary, and refusals escaped the effect as bare OSError (measured: when 2 processes land on the same target at the same instant, in 184-196 of 200 rounds = 92-98% the losing side falls over with FileExistsError; all 3 container-refusal forms passed straight through). The laying physics also changed from 'look, then link' to 'fire symlink(2) and re-read samefile on FileExistsError' — no lock is added (the home spans processes). The single definition point for the spellings is the FS-SYMLINK-* constants in effects.hy, and the set each function can return is also declared as FS-ENSURE-SYMLINK-STATES / FS-LINK-ARTIFACT-STATES. refused-by-container for a required artifact (claude's transcript / codex's rollout) is the typed reject transplant_refused (R9) — the transcript exists, so transcript_not_discoverable is not applied.] The owning profile is known from the source row's recorded fact (effective_identity) — no registry scan is introduced. The transplant carries only the conversation (transcript), not auth (auth is the binding's responsibility — measured that claude credentials are separated in the Keychain per CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR). Note that the transplant is not a revivability decision (that decision is only the stored fact, per R1) — it is physical preprocessing for hosting, a separate layer from the kill / reap decision surface of law revivability-is-stored-fact.")
     (rule R8 "Boundary verification is the caller's responsibility (added 2026-08-11): sessionhost does not verify a binding's eligibility (company/personal account fit, availability). Boundary rules are under the ACP engine's jurisdiction (ACP ADR 0068 R3), and the contract is that the caller passes only bindings whose eligibility has been judged. Adding boundary checks to sessionhost is a duplicate implementation (a split of the decision's home) and is forbidden — sessionhost checks only the binding's shape (admission) and the transcript physics (R7).")
     (rule R9 "Typed error_code vocabulary (added 2026-08-11): resume / fork admission rejects put a stable error_code, aligned with the RpcHostError family, on the wire — one_live_incarnation / identity_unknown / transcript_not_discoverable / kind_not_supported (effects.hy RESUME-ERR-* is the vocabulary's home; same family as koine's typed string code adopt_target_not_found). Machine consumers (the ACP Haskell client) match on the code, not on message substrings. Existing message wording stays unchanged for backward compatibility. The program layer raises ResumeRejected(code, message), and host dispatch maps it to the envelope's error_code. [2026-08-18 addendum: added workdir_not_found (R10) to the vocabulary.] [2026-09-22 addendum: added transplant_refused (R7 revision) to the vocabulary — the moment when the transcript was resolved but the container refused the laying. The existing 5 terms all mean 'not found', and applying one of them to a refusal sends operators searching for a transcript that is not missing. The message carries the FsSymlinkOutcome detail (syscall and errno).]")
     (rule R10 "The physical premises of an order are admission facts (added 2026-08-18 — the root fix for the total production resume failure, 91/91): before creating a host location, resume / fork checks (a) that the target work_dir (fixed to the source copy per R4) exists as a directory, and (b) that the conversation transcript is resolvable by the real CLI's discovery physics; a failure is a typed reject with zero side effects (no row created, tmux untouched, no symlink laid). (a) failing = workdir_not_found (new code). Because tmux silently substitutes $HOME for a missing start-directory, without this check claude's cwd-keyed conversation resolution, the trust pre-seed key, and the transplant laying key all diverge from the actual cwd, turning into an anonymous death as a 120s budget expiry (no-agent-frame). (b) extends R7's transplant check to same-home as well = transcript_not_discoverable (existing code). Per-kind physics: claude = existence of projects/<mangle(canonical work_dir)>/<conversation.session_id>.jsonl (a symlink is judged by its target). codex = if rollout_path is recorded in conversation_json, its existence (rows without the record are passed unchecked, since the CLI may resolve them by scanning its own home's sessions/ — the discovery physics are a home scan and cwd-independent). session.launch also checks (a) loudly before any side effect (resume reuses the launch program, so this acts as a backstop and also closes the isomorphic collapse for fresh launches). As a second layer, the startup gate terminates the CLI's conversation-resolution-failure screen (claude 'No conversation found with session ID' / codex 'no rollout found for thread id') immediately with the conversation-not-found class without waiting for the budget (added to the closed vocabulary of ADR-DOE-AGENTS-011 — a safeguard against TOCTOU and unknown paths, not a substitute for the admission check). Silently degrading an unresolvable resume order into a new conversation is forbidden — it violates the semantics of resume (continuing the same conversation), and the policy decision of whether to continue belongs to the caller (the ACP engine — direction declaration resume-on-failover-a64d9d). Checking work_dir does not contradict the existing law revivability-is-stored-fact: that one is the kill / reap decision surface (reads only rows), this one is the hosting order surface (do not create a broken host location — the same layer as moving R7 earlier).")
     (rule R11 "Where durable state attached to a conversation lives is determined by the conversation id (added 2026-09-20 — the root fix for the split of auto-memory): transcript / sessions-index / session-env / file-history follow the conversation across homes via R7's laying, but Claude Code's **auto-memory** alone was not in this convoy. The memory location was merely a side effect of CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (`<config dir>/projects/<mangled cwd>/memory/`), and doeff builds the config dir from the custody store's account (charter-with-grant). ⇒ The effective key became the pair 'account × working directory', **which nobody declared**: (a) every profile switch splits one conversation into a different location, (b) separate conversations placed on the same account share one location, and (c) when the same conversation moves between an isolated worktree and the main checkout, it splits into a third. Measured 2026-09-20 (company Mac, read-only): 30 homes; two consecutive turns of the same conversation read two locations with 0 overlap, and a memory written 15 minutes earlier did not exist from the next turn on. ⇒ Make the location a single point of declaration: the decision is one pure function judgment.memory-home-of (`<memory root>/<conversation id>` — neither account nor working directory is **among the arguments**); the value is declared in one field, AgentdSettings.memory_root (the default is derived the same way as homes-root and lies **outside** the credential home — placing it inside the home would change the location whenever the account changes, bringing back exactly the defect being fixed); and the spelling handed to the container lives in one place, impls/claude_code.hy. It is set in the charter on **every** arm that wakes the seat's process, regardless of whether a grant is lent (memory is not a credential). ⚠ The arms are not 3 but **4** (2026-09-21 addendum): besides launch / resume / rehydrate there is **the continuation of an exited process** (headless.continue-headless-process). claude's headless always exits at the end of a turn (stage 12 lane 12e), so from the second turn of a conversation onward only this 4th arm is taken — with the note still counting 3 arms, putting the location and the books in the charter sent **every ordinary turn** back to the default location (measured on a pool pod: 44 books in ACP rows versus 0 files in the location and no index either). The 4th arm has no charter, so the send for that turn (session.send's turn_charter) carries the same field, and the container-side write-out is closed in one point that does not branch by arm (interface effect HydrateMemoryHome → impls/claude_code.hy claude-hydrate-memory-home). ⚠ A further waking arm was added on 2026-09-23: **rebuild** (the arm that places a transcript assembled from the conversation record into the home and continues with `claude --resume`). This arm too goes through the single charter-building point (judgment.incarnation-charter-of) and the book fill (agentd.memory-files-for-turn) like the other waking arms, and carries the location in SessionLaunch's charter — the shape that does not go green unless whoever adds an arm names its location port is held by MEMORY-HOME-CARRIER-OF in sessionhost_acp_memory_home_deftests.hy (reflected from effects.NextArm). ⚠ Do not tilt the fix toward 'copy it onto the row' (moving it into policy.LAUNCH-FLAG-KEYS, stacking it on the row's launch_overlay): the source of truth is the ACP row (law ACP 575b1e), and a copy on the row becomes a second source of truth and rots. semgrep doeff-agents-turn-carried-key-must-not-become-a-launch-flag forbids that shape. deftest: sessionhost_charter_reaches_the_seat_deftests.hy test-declared-charter-keys-reach-the-seat-on-the-continue-arm, test-the-seat-writes-one-file-per-book-and-the-index-on-the-continue-arm; sessionhost_acp_memory_rows_deftests.hy test-a-warm-turn-carries-the-home-and-the-books-to-the-seat-too. CLI physics frozen by live firing (2026-09-20): the effective setting spelling is `autoMemoryDirectory`; `memoryDir` is merely an internal property name of the CLI, and passing it is silently ignored and the default location is created. Inline JSON in `--settings` takes effect as flagSettings ahead of userSettings (env `CLAUDE_COWORK_MEMORY_PATH_OVERRIDE` takes effect even earlier, but we use the setting spelling, which is a public key with a description). Resolution is **the first one found wins**, in the order policySettings → flagSettings → (only in a trusted worktree) localSettings / projectSettings → userSettings (confirmed by reading the 2.1.278 implementation — 2026-09-20). ⇒ The only thing that can sit on top of the adopted form is **exactly the administrator settings (policySettings)**: if the company deploys `autoMemoryDirectory` in `/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json` (on Linux `/etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json`), the location setting is silently overridden. When the symptom (conversation memory splitting again) appears, the first thing to check is whether this one file exists; on the company Mac on 2026-09-20 both were absent. Note that the CLI deliberately ignores placing it in `.claude/settings.json` committed to the repo (projectSettings) (the setting's description: 'Ignored if set in projectSettings (checked-in .claude/settings.json) for security') — a future change that moves this declaration into a settings file cannot use that route. Not a single existing location is deleted or moved: a mechanical merge cannot determine authorship (memory files have no author field, and multiple conversations used one home simultaneously), so the new location starts empty, and memories that were not hit simply remain in their original place and stop being read. codex is out of scope (codex's working state is a matter for the profile dir, and it has no location corresponding to claude's auto-memory). Continuity across machines (the memory root is a local file system, so when a conversation moves to another machine it becomes a separate copy) is outside the scope of this R — it is to be set up separately.")]
  :laws
    [(law conversation-outlives-incarnation
       :statement "durable_identity => conversation_ref_stored_in_session_rows; terminal_session_rows_never_reactivated"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "UPDATE a terminal row's status to running to 'revive' the session")
          (counterexample "do not store conversation identity on the row, and derive it from the pane / tmux session name / FS each time it is needed")])
     (law one-live-incarnation-per-conversation
       :statement "resume => reject_when_nonterminal_incarnation_exists_for_same_conversation"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "allow 2 live incarnations of the same conversation, both writing to the same transcript")])
     (law revivability-is-stored-fact
       :statement "kill_or_reap_decision => reads_session_rows_only; never_probes_fs_or_cli_at_decision_time"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "just before kill, query the FS for the existence of the rollout file to judge revivability")])
     (law resume-physics-has-one-home
       :statement "resume_fork_argv_and_transplant_paths => single_kind_impl_module_in_sessionhost_impls"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "conductor / orch / the handler layer assembles '--fork-session' or 'codex resume' argv literals on its own")
          (counterexample "the control plane or host dispatch lays transplant symlinks for projects/<mangled key>/ or sessions/<Y/M/D>/ on its own without going through the kind impl")])
     (law transplant-carries-conversation-not-auth
       :statement "cross_binding_resume => transplants_transcript_artifacts_only; auth_material_never_copied_or_linked"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "the transplant symlinks or copies .credentials.json / auth.json / Keychain material into the target home")
          (counterexample "instead of a binding, link the whole auth home together with the transcript to create a resume that 'looks logged in'")])
     (law boundary-checks-live-in-the-caller
       :statement "binding_eligibility_verdict => acp_engine_owned_adr0068_r3; sessionhost_never_reimplements_boundary_rules"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "sessionhost judges the company/personal fit of a binding's config_dir / codex_home and rejects it (a split of the decision's home — a duplicate implementation of ACP ADR 0068 R3)")])
     (law resume-rejects-are-machine-readable
       :statement "resume_admission_reject => stable_error_code_on_wire(one_live_incarnation | identity_unknown | transcript_not_discoverable | kind_not_supported | workdir_not_found); consumers_never_match_message_substrings"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "the ACP client classifies failures by a substring of the error message ('one-live-incarnation')")
          (counterexample "a change in reject message wording breaks machine consumers (= the wording, not the code, has become the contract)")])
     (law resume-premises-verified-at-admission
       :statement "resume_or_fork_order => workdir_exists(source.work_dir) and transcript_discoverable(kind_physics); premise_failure_is_typed_reject_with_zero_side_effects; never_silently_degrade_to_new_conversation"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "the total production failure of 2026-08-16 to 17: ACP ordered resume failover into a deleted workspace, sessionhost passed work_dir to tmux unchecked → tmux silently substituted $HOME → claude's cwd-keyed conversation resolution failed across the board ('No conversation found') → 120s budget expiry no-agent-frame. 91 orders / 0 completed, across 16 profiles, 20/22 bindings polluted with cooldown (fleet-stall-steward v143)")
          (counterexample "pass a same-home resume with zero FS checks 'because the transplant does not fire' — resuming a row that died at startup (conversation identity minted, transcript not yet materialized) falls into the real CLI's loud death")
          (counterexample "silently degrade a resume order for an unresolvable UUID into a new conversation (a freshly minted --session-id) — the caller wrongly believes 'the conversation was continued', and the loss of context becomes silent")
          (counterexample "cure the symptom with a change that only shortens the 120s budget expiry — the order still goes through, and broken host locations (failed rows + tmux debris) keep being created")])
     (law auto-memory-home-is-keyed-by-the-conversation
       :statement "conversation_scoped_durable_state_location => derived_from_conversation_id_only(memory_root + conversation_id); never_from_custody_account_or_credential_home_or_working_directory; stamped_on_every_waking_arm(launch | resume | rehydrate | rebuild)"
       :counterexamples
         [(counterexample "leave the auto-memory location to a side effect of the credential home (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR = <homes-root>/claude/<account>) — the location changes the moment the custody store lends a different account, and one conversation's memory splits across multiple homes (measured 2026-09-20: 30 homes, the two locations read by two consecutive turns of the same conversation overlapped in 0 entries)")
          (counterexample "place the memory root **inside** the credential home (<homes-root>/claude/<account>/…) — even if the key is built from the conversation id, the location changes when the account changes, and the same defect returns")
          (counterexample "mix the working directory into the key — a different location sprouts every time the same conversation moves between an isolated worktree (~/.worktrees/…) and the main checkout")
          (counterexample "set the location on only some of the waking arms (e.g. launch only) — memory goes to the default location only on turns where the arm is resume, and it peels off with no error and no condition visible (isomorphic to how the 2026-09-15 attachment failed)")
          (counterexample "assemble the spelling handed to the container without confirming it by a check — `memoryDir` is an internal property name of the CLI; passing it as a setting is silently ignored and the default location is created (live firing 2026-09-20)")])]
  :enforcement
    [(defsemgrep no-resume-fork-argv-outside-kind-impl
       :languages ["generic"]
       :pattern "--fork-session"
       :message "The argv physics of resume / fork are owned solely by the kind module in sessionhost impls/ (ADR-DOE-AGENTS-006 R3 / law resume-physics-has-one-home). Do not assemble this flag literal elsewhere; yield the BuildResume effect. Legitimate occurrences inside impls/ are handled by the installed rule's paths exclusion."
       :bad ["cmd = [\"claude\", \"--resume\", session_id, \"--fork-session\"]"]
       :good ["(<- argv (build-resume agent-type params))"])
     (defsemgrep no-transplant-path-literals-outside-kind-impl
       :languages ["generic"]
       :pattern "file-history"
       :message "The path physics of cross-binding transplant (claude's 4 pairs: transcript / sessions-index.json / session-env / file-history; codex's rollout relative path) are owned solely by the kind module in sessionhost impls/ (ADR-DOE-AGENTS-006 R7 / law resume-physics-has-one-home). Do not assemble this path literal elsewhere; yield the TransplantConversation effect. Legitimate occurrences inside impls/ are handled by the installed rule's paths exclusion."
       :bad ["target = f\"{config_dir}/file-history/{sid}\""]
       :good ["(<- transplanted (transplant-conversation agent-type params))"])
     (defsemgrep no-auto-memory-dir-spelling-outside-kind-impl
       :languages ["generic"]
       :pattern "autoMemoryDirectory"
       :message "The setting spelling that hands the auto-memory location to the container is owned solely by the kind module in sessionhost impls/ (ADR-DOE-AGENTS-006 R11 / law auto-memory-home-is-keyed-by-the-conversation). The location is decided at the single point judgment.memory-home-of and carried by the charter's `memory_dir` field — assembling this spelling elsewhere creates an undeclared second location. Legitimate occurrences inside impls/ and in checks that pin the spelling are handled by the installed rule's paths exclusion."
       :bad ["settings = {\"autoMemoryDirectory\": f\"{config_dir}/projects/{cwd}/memory\"}"]
       :good ["(setv memory-dir (.get params \"memory_dir\"))"])]
  :plans ["docs/adr/defadr_doeff_agents_006_conversation_resume_fork.hy"
          "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/store.hy (conversation_json / generation / lineage columns and the machine surface of terminal irreversibility)"
          "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/effects.hy (BuildResume + 2026-08-11: TransplantConversation / FsLinkArtifact / RESUME-ERR-* vocabulary)"
          "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/impls/claude_code.hy (--session-id minting is current, + resume / fork argv + claude-transplant-conversation)"
          "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/impls/codex.hy (identity capture by rollout discovery + resume / fork argv + codex-transplant-conversation)"
          "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/host.hy (session.resume / session.fork dispatch + shared admit-expected-result + ResumeRejected→error_code mapping)"
          "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/policy.hy (capability advertisement + admission + shared incarnation program)"
          "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/launch.hy (resume-session extensions for binding / new_session_id / expected_result + ResumeRejected)"
          "packages/doeff-agents/src/doeff_agents/_sessionhost/substrate.hy (FsLinkArtifact — semantic port of share.py link_session_artifact)"
          "agora-controllers controllers/agent_task (the new maintainer of R11: the single point that decides the location by conversation id, and its check. Withdrew from doeff together with agentd [sessionhost/acp/judgment.hy, acp/effects.py, sessionhost_acp_memory_home_deftests.hy])"
          "packages/doeff-agents/conformance (fake CLI resume / fork contract + loud-failure consistency + S21 cross-binding scenario + resume-physics Phase 0 probe document)"])
